SUMMARY:Avery Creek-Clawhammer-Twin Falls  7.4 miles\, 1000 ft
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Time:** Wednesday June 17th. Pro
 mpt 8:00 departure from Mills River Ingles\n**Place to Meet**: **Mills Riv
 er Ingles\, 3338 Boylston Hwy**: Directions: I-26 Exit on NC-280 West\, Ai
 rport Road--- 4.3 miles to the Ingles on the right. Meet in front of gas p
 umps\, closest to Boylston Hwy. Mark's cell: 239-777-4743. Alternate meet 
 site--trailhead at the riding stables---see below for directions. (8:30 if
  meeting at the trailhead)\n**Description**: Shaded\, lots of steam crossi
 ngs with bridges in various states of disrepair. May be muddy. Beautiful l
 unch spot at the Falls. Hike along FS Rd 477 to Avery Creek Trail on right
 . Rock hop across Avery Creek then\, at the intersection turn Right onto C
 lawhammer trail (Blue). Left on FS 5058. Left on Buckhorn Gap Trail (Orang
 e) At intersection of Twin Falls Trail (Yellow) go Right to Falls and a sn
 ack break. Return to Buckhorn Gap Trail as it follows Avery Creek to the r
 ight. Right onto Avery Creek Trail. Then left on FS Rd 477 to cars. Type: 
 Lollipop Max elev 3225'. Avg moving pace 2.4 mph. Dogs welcome if on a lea
 sh.\n**As usual\, option of grabbing a beer and/or lunch after the hike!**
 \n\n**\\*\\*Courtesy** (Please read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you 
 \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your 
 status to "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 24 ho
 urs so that wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please please PLE
 ASE don't be a no-show.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event
  involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup si
 te. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm that they
  have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and sup
 plies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike
  organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate
  all risks. By signing up for this event\, participant understands and agr
 ees.
